    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nFollowing the existing derived-field pattern (`MembershipNumber`, `MembershipLevel`), the `checkDigit` is computed as a pure function of `customerCode`, keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **New `CheckDigit.java`** \u2014 a small, isolated helper class (like `MembershipNumber`) with a single static `of(String)` method doing the Luhn computation. As a fresh single-purpose class its surrounding complexity (`WMC_other`) is ~0.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line: `checkDigit \u2192 CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`. One changed line on a low-`WMC_other` interface, matching the sibling mappings exactly.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` schema property (integer 0\u20139, read-only) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field. No functions touched here.\n\nNo existing method grew and no large class was edited \u2014 behaviour was added as small cohesive units. The acceptance test (`coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`) recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and matches the returned `checkDigit`.",
